{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Then we went to Giessen, a pleasant city and surroundings, with two nice castles in the neighborhood. Here I was with three confreres: the Giessen professor of philosophy—Snell?—the Marburg professor of the same, Creuzer?, a cousin of the Heidelberg one—and an extraordinary professor of theology, a man of striving, insight, and cultivation. But how insipid those my nearer confreres had been, I had to overlook, as the Giessen one immediately led us to wine and treated us with very good vintage. In Giessen was the parting point for those who went to Frankfurt, among whom, as we had agreed at the start, I was not, all the less as I would otherwise have spent longer in the company up to now. My young teaching colleague, the Israelite, however, stuck with me; we followed the Lahn. Weilburg has a romantic location, a beautiful, vegetation-rich, narrow valley, pleasant bends of the Lahn—and also, as a former princely residence, nice houses."}}],"created":1795080141,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":216,"prompt_tokens":311,"total_tokens":527,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-SXZcX0GrlrEOQ4UikJjbFLnFQWwMZv4O","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":311,"prompt_ms":559.26,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.7982636655948552,"prompt_per_second":556.0919786861209,"predicted_n":216,"predicted_ms":5158.967,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.995195348837207,"predicted_per_second":41.67500974516798}}